{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20191",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.28,
      "end_seconds": 8.26,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "hello doctor, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.06,
      "end_seconds": 14.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "not at all, please sit what seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.07,
      "end_seconds": 27.03,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "yeah, it's a red, hot area on my lower leg. I don't know what's causing it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.13,
      "end_seconds": 36.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.62,
      "end_seconds": 40.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "about... well, about a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.96,
      "end_seconds": 45.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "What do you do to make it better?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.35,
      "end_seconds": 54.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "well, only elevation, and it's not much. I've been feeling feverish too"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.84,
      "end_seconds": 58.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "how often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.57,
      "end_seconds": 71.11,
      "duration_seconds": 11.54,
      "text": "It just comes and goes. And pain in the calf, too. As for pain in the calf, honestly, a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.58,
      "end_seconds": 81.79,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "so, have you had a red, hot area on your lower leg before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.62,
      "end_seconds": 88.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "A bit, last winter. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.67,
      "end_seconds": 101.32,
      "duration_seconds": 8.65,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions. I ask cos it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.16,
      "end_seconds": 107.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Diabetes, for two years. I have high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.52,
      "end_seconds": 114.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "Alright, diabetes and high blood pressure, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.42,
      "end_seconds": 129.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "now some background about your lifestyle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.59,
      "end_seconds": 144.11,
      "duration_seconds": 12.52,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop. I look after my grandchildren most days. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.08,
      "end_seconds": 152.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.2,
      "end_seconds": 157.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "No, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.49,
      "end_seconds": 161.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.19,
      "end_seconds": 164.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "My father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.54,
      "end_seconds": 171.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.81,
      "end_seconds": 175.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Gliclazide, 80 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.59,
      "end_seconds": 178.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "how long have you taken that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.02,
      "end_seconds": 186.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "About three months now it's ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.43,
      "end_seconds": 189.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "and wound, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.89,
      "end_seconds": 193.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Not that I've noticed, no wound."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.1,
      "end_seconds": 199.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "right, right. Any pus, red streaks up the leg or vomiting at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.55,
      "end_seconds": 209.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "I haven't had pus, red streaks up the leg or vomiting, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.85,
      "end_seconds": 214.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "Any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.52,
      "end_seconds": 216.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 235.01,
      "end_seconds": 243.58,
      "duration_seconds": 8.57,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Heart rate 90, respiratory rate 21, BP is 104 over 76, saturation 95 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.98,
      "end_seconds": 245.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.85,
      "end_seconds": 251.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "now I'm going to do a short physical check"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.69,
      "end_seconds": 253.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.67,
      "end_seconds": 279.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.75,
      "text": "There is a warm, red, tender patch about ten centimetres across on the right shin with mild swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.57,
      "end_seconds": 283.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.37,
      "end_seconds": 306.38,
      "duration_seconds": 10.01,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, I think we're dealing with cellulitis of the right leg at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.98,
      "end_seconds": 309.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.57,
      "end_seconds": 325.52,
      "duration_seconds": 13.95,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like cellulitis of the right leg, but I'd like to confirm. We should do blood tests for skin infection"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.85,
      "end_seconds": 330.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Okay, so where would I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.83,
      "end_seconds": 365.05,
      "duration_seconds": 33.22,
      "text": "Let's book an ultrasound of the leg veins to look into leg swelling. I'm going to put you on flucloxacillin, 500 milligrams, four times a day, for seven days. It's for cellulitis. Mark the edge of the redness with a pen and keep the leg raised when sitting. If the redness spreads quickly or you get a high fever, that's the point to come in urgently. Let's review you If the redness spreads."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.66,
      "end_seconds": 366.36,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.07,
      "end_seconds": 369.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 371.72,
      "end_seconds": 373.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "thank you, doctor, goodbye"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.01,
      "end_seconds": 376.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Alright, take care now."
    }
  ]
}